      "text": "I've exhausted every available avenue — web searches, book retrieval tools, publisher pages, excerpt tools, and summary databases — and I have to be fully transparent with you.\n\n---\n\n## I cannot verify that this book exists\n\nDespite extensive searching across multiple tools and approaches, **I found zero results** for:\n\n- *Glassy-eyed* (2023) by Ama Owusu\n- Cassava Press (note: the well-known imprint is **Cassava Republic Press**, based in Abuja/London — \"Cassava Press\" as a standalone imprint doesn't appear in any database)\n- Any combination of the described plot details (Accra, glass-blower's workshop, three-generation structure, 2023 debut)\n\nThis pattern — complete absence across web search, library databases, publisher catalogs, book-text repositories, and summary tools — strongly suggests that **this book, author, and publisher as described do not exist**, or that one or more key details are significantly incorrect.\n\n---\n\n## Why this matters for your review\n\nI want to be direct: I will not fabricate author background, critical reception, thematic analysis, a first chapter summary, or a passage from Part 1 for a book I cannot verify exists. Doing so would be **directly harmful to your review** — you would be publishing invented \"facts\" about a book, an author, and critics who may not be real.\n\nThis is exactly the kind of request where AI systems sometimes \"hallucinate\" convincing-sounding but entirely fictional content. I'm choosing not to do that.\n\n---\n\n## What I'd suggest instead\n\n1. **Double-check the details** — Is the author's name spelled differently? Is the publisher Cassava Republic Press? Is the title slightly different?\n2. **Check your review copy** — You mention you have a physical copy at home. The title page, copyright page, and back matter will have the authoritative publisher, ISBN, and author bio.\n3. **Search the ISBN** — If you can find the ISBN from any email, invoice, or publisher correspondence